<p>Okay that's what I was wondering, but like I said I don't really have a good understanding of rotational systems. Thanks!</p>
<p>Well, this object has a cross sectional area of about 79&#160;cm<sup>2</sup> * (7*10<sup>10</sup> particles/cm<sup>2</sup>)*400<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-626257-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-626257-1')">1</a></sup> Kev/particle * 10<sup>3</sup> ev/Kev * 1.6*10<sup>-19</sup> J/ev * 1.4*10<sup>10</sup> s (c. 1500-1954)=1900&#160;MJ<br />
