<p>Edit2: 700&#160;J/kg°C*1&#160;kg * 20°C= 1400&#160;J. If it absorbs that every second from collisions with air molecules that's 1400J/s*1.4*10<sup>10</sup> s=1.96 * 10<sup>7</sup> MJ. That's only half a percent of of a Mt equivalent. I guess having a perfect energy sponge is less impressive than I'd imagine.</p>
